<title>CHINA: China slaughters more pigs and cattle in H1.</title>
<headline>China slaughters more pigs and cattle in H1.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>China slaughtered 260 million pigs in the first half of the year, up 7.1 percent from a year ago and 18.0 million head of cattle, up 14.6 percent, the Farmers' Daily said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Slaughtered sheep and goats reached 84.87 million head in the period, up 14.6 percent compared with the year-ago period, it said, quoting figures from the State Statistical Bureau.</p>
<p>At end-June, China had a total of 442 million pigs, up 3.2 percent compared with the year-ago period, it said. It gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (86) 10-6532-1921; Fax (86) 10-6532-4978</p>
</text>
